WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.690
TV on!

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:03.410
GA's about to begin!

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:04.800
Go! AsakaraTV!

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:05.680
It's today's fortune.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.720
Today's good luck is... "Ora ora ora!"

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:09.290
And then it's... "Oyo yo~n"

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.140
Next it's...

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:11.090
Huh?

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.510
Hey!

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:49.270
<b>Pat</b>

00:01:49.510 --> 00:01:50.480
Yo!

00:01:54.590 --> 00:01:55.570
Hey!

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:57.580
<b>Bop!</b>

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:02.790
Hey.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:02.630
<b>Poink</b>

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.370
Good morning!

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.830
Who's 'It' now?

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:06.740
Kisaragi!

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.340
What! Since when?

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:09.870
Yay, you're 'It'. You're 'It'!

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:11.240
Hurry up and tag us!

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.080
Huh? Oh! Yes, sorry!

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.220
What's wrong?

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.600
Time out!

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.720
We're playing tag right now.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.000
And since Kisaragi-chan was 'It'...

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.330
And I touched her...

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:31.270
I should tell you,

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:32.780
I'm running away at full speed!

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:33.830
Even though it's a game.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:36.600
I wanna see Kyouju
 running at full speed!

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.570
This is the last episode 
of the drama Tomokane-dono

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.270
asked me to bring last night...

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.930
If you don't come and get it
now I’m taking it home.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.610
I won't run or hide! Sorry! Sorry!

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:51.620
<b>Tag Collage</b>

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.670
What are you doing, Kisaragi?

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:58.140
Why stand up a 
painting board here?

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.840
Oh, Namiko-san.

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:02.750
Since I'm bad at running away,
I was hiding a little bit.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.580
Come get me!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.400
Why are you doing this 
early in the morning?

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.790
 Huff huff

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:09.680
Noda-chan had this idea...

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:11.130
So now we're all playing tag.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.120
Change!

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:17.130
<b>Change!</b>

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:13.860
Starting now, we're playing Color Tag!

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:14.400
Cheater!

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.250
We were all playing tag!

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:16.110
Past tense, right?

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:17.140
Honestly, that little princess...

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:21.150
It

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:20.360
In color tag, first the person 
who's 'It' chooses a color.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.150
Red!

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:24.170
If you're touching the indicated 
color then you're safe.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.650
If you're tagged while not touching 
the color then you're out!

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:29.460
I never heard about this before.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.380
Then you might struggle in the beginning.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:32.920
Struggle ("Kurou") contains 
the word Black ("Kuro")

00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:33.370
Good luck!

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.600
The next class is perfect for color tag!

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:40.590
'Cuz you can mix up

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:42.590
essentially any color you want
 using your art supplies!

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.400
Is that fair?

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.400
Now we have nothing to fear 
from the person who's 'It'!

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:50.350
Did you borrow my white 
and yellow poster paints?

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.960
I wonder if you remembered 
to buy your own for today.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.210
Gimme!

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:54.210
Yellow!

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:57.780
All right! Here comes a counterattack!

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:58.520
Orange!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.140
Where's orange? Orange!

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:01.020
O- Orange!

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.350
Hey, tag!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:06.160
Kyouju, you're 'It'.

00:04:09.110 --> 00:04:10.930
Class is starting.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.320
I'll deal with it later.

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.240
I'll get some water.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.470
<b> Time for recess.</b>

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.170
 Collages, Necessary Materials: ...

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.370
Whatcha doing?

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.800
I was checking to make sure

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:27.230
I hadn't forgotten anything for class.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.610
Oh! How studious!

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:31.100
And, unusually, I'll be studious as well!

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.380
Now praise me!

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:35.890
For materials, I brought 
old magazines from home.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:38.060
And I even noticed that 
I forgot a box cutter

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:39.850
and glue so I bought them along the way!

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:42.140
But you did forget things, after all.

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:43.390
Now praise me!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:44.600
Okay, let's check.

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.400
I'll go with you to the supply 
shop if you'd like.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:53.160
Kisaragi-chan, what materials did you bring

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.590
for your collage?

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.470
Ads and wrapping paper.

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.580
Oh! This sofa is cute!

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.420
There are some colorful ones as well,

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:05.150
but this one is half the 
price of the other ones!

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:09.680
But synthetic leather is more 
resistant to wear and stains.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.680
In the long run you'd have 
to go with this one.

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:14.250
I guess there's that too...

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.010
Not that I was going to buy any!

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.700
The fun part is looking.

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:22.580
Like, what if I had one of these?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.040
I just let my imagination run wild.

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.610
I'm the same way.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:28.880
I know!

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:31.100
Then, let's make a thought 
collage out of our imagination!

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.840
A collage?

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.830
 Antique

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.350
If we combine the photos that Kyouju took of me

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.850
with this magazine page we get...

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:39.070
It becomes like this!

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.120
She's playing on a sofa!

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.490
We pull together all kinds of 
materials in the same way!

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.330
Like these clothes or those shoes.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:50.630
Oh, so that's why it's a "thought collage".

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.630
A clock, a table, a Jumeau 
Bisque doll, a shaded lamp!

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.640
Kisaragi-chan and Kyouju 
wear these clothes, okay?

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.070
Um, but these are men's...

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:04.900
The setting is two gentlemen 
fighting over a young lady.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.320
A rich nobleman and a poor scholar.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.450
This is starting to become 
a game of "thought house."

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:14.790
I've always wanted to become 
a lady and try this once.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.220
Excuse me, Someone.

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:18.120
That was close.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.160
There was only one glue stick 
left at the supply shop.

00:06:22.990 --> 00:06:24.640
Morning, old maid.

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:26.730
Old...! What! Who!

00:06:24.930 --> 00:06:26.730
Oh, she's the old maid.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.650
<b> Bam!</b>

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:34.720
 Given back.

00:06:28.260 --> 00:06:30.910
Owowowow. I was hit!

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.840
I'll fire that violent old maid!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.620
Moving on, Yamaguchi.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:38.290
I am hungry.

00:06:38.290 --> 00:06:40.450
Bring me something delicious.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.380
Milady has become a samurai lord.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.760
Understood!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.480
I'll test my skills with scissors!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.260
There's still lots more to come!

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.430
Kisaragi-dono has been cutting up

00:06:52.440 --> 00:07:05.250
<b> Snip snip</b>

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:57.190
nothing but sweets for some time now...

00:06:57.190 --> 00:06:58.440
At full speed.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.260
Yes!

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:02.460
Apparently the old maid of 
the house loves sweets.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.040
When she gets serious, 
nothing gets in her way, does it?

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:07.830
Namiko-san, you brought 
materials too, right?

00:07:07.830 --> 00:07:09.200
Let's play together!

00:07:09.500 --> 00:07:13.390
All I brought were some 
magazines and old newspapers.

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.910
Hey! It is I, Tomokane!

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.230
Oh! This might be interesting to paste in.

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:23.320
What are these?

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:24.820
 "Once in a Day"
TV Series influenced by GAG Drama

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.720
Clippings from TV series.

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.440
 "Burning Red Rose" 
 "Two-face Women"

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:28.560
Huh? This looks like a daytime soap...

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.900
I also tried making one of these.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.750
 Tonight, watch your back.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:31.760
Suspense!

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.490
What's this what's this! Looks fun!

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:34.690
Let me play!

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.530
Oh! Some stranger has barged in.

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:38.580
You're doing it wrong, Tomokane.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.880
It's a collage so you need materials.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.710
Oh really? Let's see...

00:07:44.410 --> 00:07:47.180
All right! Is this okay?

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:49.380
Who are you?

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:51.670
I've finally discovered your evil hideout!

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:52.980
We're the evil ones?!

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:55.070
What materials did you bring?

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.510
Video game strategy books

00:07:56.510 --> 00:07:57.760
and my brother's hobby model magazine.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:07:59.890
Super small fusion engine with

00:07:59.890 --> 00:08:01.260
3,000,000 horse power!

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.930
Top speed Mach 3.8!

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:04.410
Equipped with a beam cannon and

00:08:04.410 --> 00:08:05.780
mega particle weapons!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.300
This is turning out really weird.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.570
Here, Masa, paste this.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:12.670
<b>Plastic Models 60% Off!</b>

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:15.170
What! I'm super cheap all of a sudden!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:18.220
Namiko-san cut it from an ad.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:19.440
I'll do one too!

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.810
<b> Antique Model</b>

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:22.810
Hey, hey, hey! Cut it out!

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.180
<b> No more rebounds! 
Get slim in a week.</b>

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.180
This doesn't even make sense!

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.790
<b> New virus discovered!</b>

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:27.790
Who pasted this on?!

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:30.450
First bell.

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:33.560
The real lessons are starting.

00:08:33.560 --> 00:08:36.030
I guess the collage game ends here.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:38.960
So, do we end it like this?

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:41.670
I think this is better.

00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.030
How is that different?

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:48.620
Since half our classes 
are for art and design,

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.640
on top of being a private school,

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.840
a lot of money goes into

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.760
art supplies and art exhibition fees.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:58.580
What made you guys want to come here?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.100
Why GA?

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:01.340
Well, that would have to be

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:03.300
because we love art and drawing.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.560
Why are you asking all of a sudden?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:04.560
And fashion!

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.370
Because this is the only 
school in our prefecture

00:09:07.370 --> 00:09:09.530
that offers general art classes.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:13.650
For me, since my sister was a student here.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.430
She doesn't go here anymore though.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.080
Me too, me too!

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.000
My sister is in the regular school.

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:22.930
I have an old friend who's 
two years ahead of me.

00:09:22.930 --> 00:09:24.570
That's why I came.

00:09:25.190 --> 00:09:29.460
<b> 1 Year Ago</b>

00:09:26.920 --> 00:09:29.810
Kisa-chan, you like art, right?

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.160
I'll show you around this school.

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:35.020
<b>Azai High School</b>

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.520
This is my first time
 at a private school!

00:09:40.520 --> 00:09:41.760
We'll start at the front.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.160
In front of the entrance is a an ancient Haniwa.

00:09:43.530 --> 00:09:44.530
<b> Ta-da!</b>

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:48.900
It's said to have some sort 
of demon-repelling properties,

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.530
but isn't he cute?

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:51.820
<b>Ooh</b>

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.220
There are lots of Haniwa 
all over the campus.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:57.170
Oh!! You have chickens, as well.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:09:59.140
Kisa-chan, you've actually noticed

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:00.860
something rather interesting.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:04.450
Everyone calls the chickens "chicken lords".

00:10:04.990 --> 00:10:06.350
I see...

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:09.180
The school's mascot
is the Haniwa and

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:12.430
so we have Haniwa
 all over the campus.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:15.160
Niwatori = Chicken

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:15.160
Similarly, by adding "Ha" to the beginning
of "Niwatori," it becomes "Haniwa-tori"!

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:16.130
Wow.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:19.880
Oh is that a weather vane bird up there?

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.230
That's a weather vane Haniwa!

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:22.790
I knew it!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.590
And so that's why I decided to come!

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:27.880
Wait, when? Where?

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:31.280
Which part of that story 
was your deciding factor?

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:36.440
I shall hug you meow!

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.570
My name is Awara Chikako.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.590
GA-3, art design class, third year.

00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:47.490
Hey! No running in the halls!

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.090
Something has happened and 
I'm in a bit of a rush!

00:10:50.350 --> 00:10:52.440
Buchi-san! We're in trouble!

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:53.960
What's wrong, Aa-san?

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:59.380
Quick, come listen to this or 
else we'll all be erased!!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:02.410
Were you a co-signer 
on a large unpaid loan?

00:11:02.670 --> 00:11:04.460
The fine arts club is being disbanded?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.470
That's right.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:11.980
We don't have any new 
members this year so...

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.190
What should we do, Buchi-san?!

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.020
There, there.
 Don't cry.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:17.640
Oh yeah, Buchi-san,

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:19.570
you know a freshman, right?

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.030
Oh. Yes, she's a childhood friend of mine.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.550
I wonder if she's the kind of girl

00:11:24.550 --> 00:11:25.730
that would like the fine arts club.

00:11:25.730 --> 00:11:28.110
Let's see, I think she 
strongly dislikes invitations

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.290
that involve rope and duct tape.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.500
Calm down, Aa-san.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.910
So, did you already talk it 
over with the other two?

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.740
Not yet, they weren't on 
that side of campus so...

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.910
But I sent a message to Uozumi,

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:39.540
so he should already know about it.

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:41.930
Oh, well then they must be here!

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:43.590
Or maybe, knowing 
that the club might disband,

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:45.430
they're running around desperately

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.550
searching for new members.

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:49.030
Hey, it's the president.

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:50.450
Oh! What's up president?

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.800
What! Why? President!

00:11:53.800 --> 00:11:56.070
Attacking her club members
and equipment as soon as she enters!

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:57.590
You guys are getting 
along great again today.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.160
<b>Fine arts club in session.</b>

00:11:59.160 --> 00:11:59.740
What!

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.340
Our club is about to be disbanded?

00:12:01.340 --> 00:12:03.050
So you didn't read my message after all!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:05.430
I figured this would happen eventually.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.340
I guess you guys are the 
only members this year.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:10.060
President, GA3 Awara.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:13.110
<b>Normal Department
(Special Day Student)</b>

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:12.980
Vice President, FA3 Uozumi.

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.750
KJ2, Homura.

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:14.610
<b>Manufacturing Department
(Car Servicing Class)</b>

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.430
Wait, Mizubuchi-senpai isn't a member?

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.290
No, I'm not a fine arts member.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.360
Though, I do look after Aa-san.

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.620
So there are three of us...

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.190
Four!

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:27.690
Please don't count the sketch dummy.

00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.960
So how many more do we need?

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:31.690
The rules say five,

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:34.490
but they said it's okay 
if we get one freshman.

00:12:34.490 --> 00:12:35.960
A freshman, huh.

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.040
It should work out if you 
do a mass recruitment.

00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:39.970
About that...

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.910
You actually tried that last 
spring didn't you, Awara?

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:45.060
Really?

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:46.990
That's right. 
That's why I joined.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.950
Stop! Please don't talk about it!

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:58.110
Fine Arts Club
Join!

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.450
People were saying there was this weird girl

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.450
Do you want to take everything you've ever

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.350
doing a public invitational 
in this funny Kansai accent!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.350
 thought and throw it onto a canvas?!

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:54.910
I sensed that self-destructive girl could

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:56.370
be next year’s president.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.540
She became a classroom topic of 
conversation, to say the least.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:01.090
It's not Kansai. It's Chubu!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.920
Because of that I was 
instantly characterized.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.700
Tono-sensei please do something!

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.950
Do something about it yourselves.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:10.690
<b>Sasamoto Sensei (F) Nickname "Tono"</b>

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.490
I only became this club's advisor

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.720
so I could use this room.

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.200
What a teacher.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.020
Well, I guess I'll try 
a few people in class.

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:19.030
I'll go ask my friend, too.

00:13:19.030 --> 00:13:19.690
Really?

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.980
But no rope, okay?

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:23.680
You guys. Class is about to start.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:24.820
Really?

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.890
Buchi-san, what do we have next?

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.160
Um, sketching.

00:13:28.160 --> 00:13:29.580
Going to get our art supplies

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:30.910
from our homeroom is a pain.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.510
There's a set right there, 
so let's just borrow that.

00:13:33.510 --> 00:13:34.590
I guess someone forgot it.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:37.260
Tono, you don't mind if 
I change here, do you?

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.980
<b>Next Recess</b>

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:42.270
Noda-chan, Namiko-san, run!

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:44.100
I wish they'd make recesses 15 minutes

00:13:44.100 --> 00:13:46.250
when we have class on the university campus.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:49.460
Seriously! Oh no, only three 
minutes 'til the bell.

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:51.140
Dash! Dash!

00:13:51.650 --> 00:13:55.020
All right! Let's go look 
for some GA freshmen.

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.360
It'd be nice if Kisa-chan 
was in this classroom.

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:00.130
Buchi-san, let's take this shortcut.

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.100
We'll be there in a minute.

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:01.790
Right.

00:14:01.790 --> 00:14:03.990
We somehow made it on time.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.470
It's like we just had PE.

00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:09.130
Kisa-chan!

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:11.400
Can I talk to you for a second?

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.340
Well, I talked to her about it.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:20.670
And? And? How did it go?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.670
Hmm... Well, she was very polite about it,

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:26.030
but I don't think she'll join.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:27.710
What? Why!

00:14:27.710 --> 00:14:30.680
Probably, right now, Kisa-chan

00:14:30.680 --> 00:14:33.300
is very happy with her friends.

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:36.250
I guess, no matter how 
much you like drawing,

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.340
there's no place for a fine arts club at GA.

00:14:39.340 --> 00:14:40.520
What about you guys?

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:42.900
I tried a few freshmen and sophomores,

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.030
but I didn't get many optimistic answers.

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:47.790
What about the seniors 
from the special class?

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:50.610
What senior is going to 
do something that eccentric?

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.330
Noo! What should we do!

00:14:52.330 --> 00:14:54.040
We're as good as disbanded.

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.350
Calm down, president. 
We still have a chance.

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.530
I was just in the club room

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.290
and it looks like our Tono is on the move!

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.190
Tono is?!

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.910
Yup! She was carrying the club keys and

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:03.090
what looked like a
 list of student names

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:04.820
and was headed for
 the student council.

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.660
Hold on.

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:08.340
She might just be 
planning to return them!

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.700
She had this relieved expression,

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:11.190
like she was freed of huge burden!

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:12.420
We're done for!

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:17.320
Oh, well. If I'd known 
this was going to happen,

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:20.000
then maybe I should've
 forced you to join, Buchi-san.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:23.060
You can't do that. 
Besides, I'm part of another club.

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:26.220
But Aa-san, maybe the reason 
why there aren't any

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:27.850
new members is because we 
already have fine arts classes

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.900
and the need for a club has disappeared.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.010
Maybe...

00:15:31.290 --> 00:15:35.030
If you're in GA, you're 
doing art every day.

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:36.850
And as for the club, Aa-san, 
since you're a senior

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:38.780
you'll only be in it for 
another half year anyway.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:42.910
You don't have to work so 
hard for the fine arts club.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:44.660
That's not true!

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:47.880
There are plenty of things that 
you can only do in the club.

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.780
When I was a freshman, we 
had an amazing president.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:53.600
She was called Nozaki-senpai

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:56.570
and she taught me so many 
things in just one year.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:58.740
Not just Art know-how,

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:01.540
but she taught me about 
the school's shortcuts,

00:16:01.540 --> 00:16:06.580
and which lounge seats are 
most likely to be open.

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:08.450
So that's how it was!

00:16:08.450 --> 00:16:11.280
When she graduated,

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:14.800
she entrusted the club's future 
and new recruitment to me,

00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:17.400
so I've been doing my best to...

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.500
And you've come this far, right?

00:16:20.350 --> 00:16:24.380
Even though we only have idiots for members,

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:28.710
They come every day despite the distance.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.090
Even Tono-sensei shows us

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:33.290
a different side of her than during class.

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:37.250
I loved the time I spent 
there, both then and now.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.420
So, that's why...

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:39.840
Well said, President!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:44.050
Be merry! For I bear good news, President!

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:53.740
 The doll's tag reads "Sanae-chan"

00:16:44.050 --> 00:16:45.130
Sanae-chan?!

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:46.120
Nope, it's us.

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.570
Now, now. Among us idiot members,

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.690
isn't the biggest idiot you?

00:16:51.740 --> 00:16:53.320
Both of you, hurry! 
Close the door!

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.350
Aa-san!

00:16:55.370 --> 00:16:57.030
A merger?

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:58.890
Yup. We'll merge with

00:16:58.890 --> 00:17:00.370
the other group that Tono advises.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.060
I think it's called the 
"School Lifestyle Club".

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:04.940
Well, there's a club that's 
something like that.

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:04.940
Hey, Adviser.

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:08.870
Like this one, it's a small 
club with only one member.

00:17:08.870 --> 00:17:10.960
However, thanks to their internal activities,

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:12.940
they may not be disbanded.

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.120
And, of course, since you'll be merging,

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.810
you'll be involved in both club activities.

00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:18.890
What'll it be?

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:22.320
But, this isn't something 
that I can decide alone.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:23.990
Idiot.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.470
Don't start worrying 
about how we feel now.

00:17:25.470 --> 00:17:26.430
It's creepy.

00:17:26.430 --> 00:17:27.400
It's great, right?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:29.330
This way you can keep the club 
together for a little longer.

00:17:30.220 --> 00:17:32.070
Don't cry, don't cry.

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:35.330
I'm not crying... yet.

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:37.760
But if we've decided then we should

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:39.360
talk to the other person as soon as--

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:41.450
Oh, that's okay actually.

00:17:41.450 --> 00:17:43.390
I'm president of that club.

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:45.360
I was recruited by Tono in my second year.

00:17:45.360 --> 00:17:47.680
What! Really?

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:50.140
Both clubs have been sharing 
the materials room

00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:52.330
behind the prep room anyways.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:55.260
So then it's just going 
to be the same as always.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:56.630
All that really happened today

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.690
was the president getting flustered.

00:17:57.690 --> 00:17:59.340
You're all idiots!

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:01.690
Stop attacking your members and equipment!

00:18:01.690 --> 00:18:04.260
Looks like the fine arts 
club is back to normal.

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.900
It's Art Room 2.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.840
I'll go see if we can use it.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.990
So, by the way, what does the 
School Lifestyle Club do?

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:14.170
In short...

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:15.690
How's it look, Kisaragi?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:16.590
Can we use it?

00:18:16.590 --> 00:18:19.000
It looks like it's in use.

00:18:19.000 --> 00:18:21.430
Oh! It says so right there.

00:18:19.460 --> 00:18:25.070
<b> Fine Arts Club In Session</b>

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:23.200
Hmm... the fine arts club, huh.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.080
I was in one in middle school.

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:27.000
What were they doing inside?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.380
From the looks of it,

00:18:28.380 --> 00:18:30.570
something other than club activities.

00:18:30.570 --> 00:18:33.690
But, they did seem to be very happy.

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.520
Whoever it was that complained can quit!

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.410
The game of color tag is 
officially restarted!

00:18:40.410 --> 00:18:43.450
Kyouju is it, but this time 
we have nothing to fear!

00:18:43.450 --> 00:18:47.270
Our secret weapon is our color textbook!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:49.470
Is that cheating?

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.180
Who cares?

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:52.790
It's not against the rules.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:55.370
With this, all 256 colors are within

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:57.150
our reach in an instant!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.270
Now, where is she?

00:18:58.270 --> 00:18:59.820
Even Kyouju is no match for us now!

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.950
Ikkonzome.

00:19:00.520 --> 00:19:01.950
Ikkonzome is the color of silk dyed 
with 1 Kon (600g) of Safflower.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:02.950
<b>Ikkonzome</b>

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:06.580
Also known as "Pale Orchid Pink"

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:09.060
It's a light purple-pink.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:10.690
<b>Poink</b>

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.360
<b> Tomokane is 'It'</b>

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:14.160
Damn! All right, here I go!

00:19:14.160 --> 00:19:15.010
White!

00:19:15.010 --> 00:19:15.870
White!

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:19.350
<b> White Paper</b>

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:19.370
Found it!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.360
<b>Ka-pow!</b>

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:27.310
Damn, I guess she already touched it.

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:29.380
Tagging with your fist is prohibited!

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:32.820
Shit! How about this!

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:35.380
Cyan 72%, Magenta 53%,

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:38.690
Yellow 0%, Black 50% mixed together!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.790
How are we supposed to figure that out!

00:19:40.790 --> 00:19:42.790
My chance! Prepare yourself, Noda!

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:44.030
Ah! Oh no! I'm trapped!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.440
My secret attack!

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:48.170
Noda-chan Primary Color Barrier!

00:19:48.230 --> 00:19:48.930
<b>Pow!</b>

00:19:48.880 --> 00:19:50.170
This time she went with her palm.

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.880
I wonder how many years it's been since

00:19:52.880 --> 00:19:54.500
I saw someone try a barrier in tag.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:58.420
Masa, have you heard of Ice Tag?

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.680
We called it Freeze Tag, but yes.

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:03.490
When you're tagged by someone

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:05.300
<b>It</b>

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:04.950
 Freeze

00:20:03.490 --> 00:20:05.030
who's 'It', you freeze.

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.580
When you're tagged by a friend,

00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.900
<b> Friend</b>

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:07.070
<b> Touch</b>

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.450
you can move again.

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:11.520
I kinda thought this situation was similar.

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:13.800
But in our case,

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:16.470
when you get tagged you turn into a corpse.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:20.830
Come to think of it,

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:24.830
even as a child, I was terrible at tag.

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:27.730
No matter how hard I ran and ran,

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:30.610
I was too slow to catch up to anyone else.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.290
My friends were so far away,

00:20:32.350 --> 00:20:33.860
I couldn't see their faces.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:35.610
I felt so lonely.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.880
Even though I was playing with them,

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.580
It felt like I was always running by myself.

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.590
Kisaragi-chan started crying!

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.460
It's been 157 minutes 
since Kisaragi became 'It'

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.180
and she's finally started crying!

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:50.750
You can do it, Kisaragi-chan!

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:52.710
<b>Poink</b>

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:54.880
Kyouju-san.

00:20:55.200 --> 00:20:56.790
I shall take the responsibility

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.460
of being 'It' from you
 and do away with it.

00:20:59.840 --> 00:21:01.250
So cool!

00:21:03.750 --> 00:21:05.320
Man... that was a good fight.

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:07.110
Noda-chan, hurry. Hurry!

00:21:07.400 --> 00:21:11.270
By this time we might be the 
only ones left at school.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:16.250
But why did you decide to play tag today?

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.040
Um, that's because today was the 11th.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:21.580
I'm not sure what you mean.

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:25.550
The key to good luck for 
Sagittarius today was "Tag"!

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:28.190
It was pretty challenging 
to pull off though!

00:21:28.190 --> 00:21:29.060
Wait.

00:21:29.060 --> 00:21:31.490
You had us running around all day for that?

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:32.610
Because I'm a lady!

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:33.770
Like I care!!

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:45.390
You mustn't come any closer.

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:48.660
Masa, you seem serious yet kinda crazy.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.020
And also a good person, too.

00:21:50.920 --> 00:21:52.460
<b>Pat pat</b>

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:26.940
Even when you go to the cafeteria,

00:23:26.940 --> 00:23:28.430
you need to bring entertainment, right?

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:29.620
Noda, you really don't have to

00:23:29.620 --> 00:23:30.820
do anything unnecessary this time.

00:23:30.820 --> 00:23:33.720
All right! I accept this challenge!

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:35.610
Kisaragi-dono, what's wrong?

00:23:35.080 --> 00:23:40.060
The Importance of Photography

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:39.430
I'm not good at taking photographs.
